cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "undeRfactor: What One Factor Measures When the Items Come from Two Traits"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
authors:
  - family-names: "Tomašević"
    given-names: "Aleksandar"
    affiliation: "Institute of Physics Belgrade, University of Belgrade, Serbia"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4863-6051"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/atomashevic/undeRfactor"
abstract: >-
  Tools for one-factor models fitted to items generated by two correlated
  traits. Computes the trait correlation below which the fitted factor stops
  being an equal-weight composite and follows one trait (maximum likelihood,
  unweighted least squares and WLSMV), exact population values of the
  discrepancy and of CFI, TLI, RMSEA and SRMR, the trait correlations above
  which conventional fit-index cutoffs no longer reject the one-factor model,
  the share of each trait in the fitted factor, and a check of whether item
  order or starting values change the one-factor solution in a sample.
keywords:
  - factor analysis
  - fit indices
  - unidimensionality
  - R
